{"created": "2026-07-15T04:18:54.959174+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-15T04:23:39.872488+00:00", "id": 21367800, "conceptrecid": "21318696", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21318696", "metadata": {"title": "Preliminary Summary of Harmonic Readout and c=1 Area Sweep in an AB Two-Body Closed Phase System", "publication_date": "2026-07-15", "description": "This V3 release updates the AB two-body harmonic readout and c=1 area sweep summary while keeping the original scope and claims unchanged. V3 applies the fermion-like recoil map to chi_read as the scattering-matrix factor q_out_factor. The result confirms that the harmonic acceleration-like readout frame and the chi-tau surface remain evaluable in the AB two-body closed phase system. The paper still does not claim a native inverse-area, inverse-law, or inverse-square-law derivation.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kihara, Noriaki", "affiliation": "WF System Co., Ltd.", "orcid": "0009-0004-6753-4020"}], "keywords": ["AB two-body closed phase system", "harmonic readout", "acceleration-like readout", "label-free relation", "fermion-like recoil map", "scattering matrix", "q_out_factor", "c=1 internal calibration", "chi-tau area", "wave information readout"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21315735", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21308049", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v3", "language": "eng", "license": "cc-by-4.0", "imprint_publisher": "Zenodo", "notes": "This V3 update keeps the AB two-body acceleration-readout claims unchanged. It only replaces the recoil readout implementation with chi_read = q_out_factor * chi_pass, where q_out_factor = T - R and the complete-recoil limit gives q_out_factor = -1.", "upload_type": "publication", "publication_type": "preprint", "prereserve_doi": {"doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21367800", "recid":